# Mark and Toys

## Problem Summary

Given the prices of different toys and a fixed amount of money, determine the maximum number of toys that can be purchased without exceeding the available budget.

## Approach

1. Sort the toy prices in ascending order.
2. Start with the cheapest toy.
3. Keep buying toys while the total cost does not exceed the budget.
4. Stop when the next toy cannot be purchased.
5. Return the number of toys purchased.

## Algorithm

The greedy strategy is used. We always purchase the cheapest available toy first.

## Time Complexity

O(N log N)

The sorting operation takes O(N log N) time.

## Auxiliary Space Complexity

O(log N) to O(N), depending on the sorting implementation.

## Why This Approach Is Efficient

Buying the cheapest toys first maximizes the number of toys that can be purchased within the given budget.

## Alternative Approach

Without sorting, we could repeatedly find the cheapest remaining toy. However, repeatedly searching for the minimum can take O(N²) time, making it less efficient.

